                <mxCell id="c_diff" parent="c1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontSize=13;" value="&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 16px;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Differences in short&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;1. Built: tile planning (6 files, 71 tests). Not built: everything of the image fetch.&lt;br&gt;2. No main, factory or coordinator yet; only the unit tests call the code.&lt;br&gt;3. Data passes as dictionaries (list[dict]); the flowchart uses typed objects (RawImage, GeoTIFF).&lt;br&gt;4. Protocols sit in one central file; the flowchart document defines them at the consumer.&lt;br&gt;5. The flowchart runs per bbox; the plan runs per planned tile (ID, state, sites).&lt;br&gt;6. ImageStore is new: the plan has no protocol for storing tiles yet.&lt;/font&gt;" vertex="1">
